@startuml
title SIC/XE Simulator - WebSocket Protocol
actor Frontend
participant "WebSocket /ws" as WS
participant Simulator
participant "Architecture / CPU" as CPU

Frontend -> WS : Request {id, type, payload}
WS -> Simulator : dispatch(request)

alt Run
  Simulator -> CPU : run until breakpoint/halt/input
  CPU --> Simulator : execution state/events
else Step
  Simulator -> CPU : step()
  CPU --> Simulator : ExecutionEvent[]
else Stop
  Simulator -> CPU : stop()
  CPU --> Simulator : stopped state
else Unstep
  Simulator -> CPU : restore command/history state
  CPU --> Simulator : restored state
else BreakOn
  Simulator -> CPU : register breakpoint
  CPU --> Simulator : breakpoint registered
end

Simulator --> WS : {id, result, error}
WS --> Frontend : response matched by id

note over Frontend,WS
Every request carries an id.
The frontend keeps pending promises keyed by id.
end note

note right of Simulator
Commands:
Request
Run
Step
Stop
Unstep
BreakOn
end note

@enduml
